  <ThingDef ParentName="HelghastBaseHumanMakeableGun">
    <defName>Gun_HG_StA3g</defName>
    <label>StA-3 LMG</label>
    <description>When the need for a light machine gun arose, the initial reaction from Stahl Arms was confusion; their entire design philosophy was to allow any part of a squad to suppress positions. However, initial attempts at mounting the StA-52 to vehicle hulls proved ineffective, and so the venerable StA-3 was revived. Originally commissioned by the Helghan corporation of a much younger Stahl Arms to provide a light vehicle mounted machine gun, the StA-3 has always been a bullet-hose. Fire rate was optimized above all. Compared to other LMGs, the StA 3 is lighter, quick to set up, and exceedingly inaccurate except at close range. The intent of the StA-3 was to suppress squad elements over a wide area. Yet, despite its shortcomings, the weapon is still used today in squad automatic rifle roles. Infantry have a love hate relationship with the gun, which has been responsible for friendly fire incidents on occasion.</description>
