  <ThingDef ParentName="HelghastBaseHumanMakeableGun">
    <defName>Gun_HG_StA6g</defName>
    <label>StA-6 HMG</label>
    <description>A bold, bulky weapon designed alongside the heavy suits Stahl co-designed with Visari, the StA-6 is never seen on any infantry unit not wearing one such suit for a simple reason: it is absolutely enormous and requires ammo fed from the suits loader systems. Firing .50 caliber depleted uranium slugs from a pressurized ammo drum at the rear of the suit- a design compromise required because of the high cyclic fire rate of this system allows it to wreak havoc on even well defended enemy positions. Intended as a mobile, urban warfare anti infantry autocannon, the StA-6 proved capable of punching through light vehicle chassis inside of 100 meters, and consistently defeated infantry armor systems. Combined with the suits exoskeleton, aim was fairly smooth, as despite a good fire rate and heavy round, the weight of the rifle itself stabilized the system. Helghan 'heavies' had a love hate relationship with this gun- even with the suit it caused long term backpain and had a bad habit of causing small bone fractures in the arms from the immense strength needed to use this firearm over an extended period. But perhaps this was a bad way to look at its performance: those health concerns only flared up because their operators killed everything and everyone they came into contact with and lived to tell about it. Few ballistic weapons in the helghan arsenal achieve the raw power and performance of this firearm.</description>
